{
  "title": "Last One",
  "hook_type": "warning",
  "cards": [
    {
      "text": "Never photograph an empty room after a wedding.",
      "scene": "dark",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1486492440844-ebc195542a40?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "rs4YQElqCV8",
      "photo_credit": "Mitchell Hollander"
    },
    {
      "text": "I've done it at the end of every wedding for six years.",
      "scene": "house",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1570905810373-a8ae44f954cb?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "fhU7X34rCAE",
      "photo_credit": "Devon MacKay"
    },
    {
      "text": "I shoot weddings for a living, and that last shot of the empty hall is my signature.",
      "scene": "table",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1768851142332-75f3d1b47452?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "cQxEJoQZ_-E",
      "photo_credit": "Matt Benson"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stacked chairs, trampled petals, one balloon drifting along the ceiling.",
      "scene": "hallway",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1769667693219-4d8e44b6a3b3?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "3S1AgG4Mq-g",
      "photo_credit": "yanzheng xia"
    },
    {
      "text": "Before I press the shutter, I always say \"Last one\" out loud. Just a habit.",
      "scene": "door",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523804427826-322aa3cfaa42?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "GhxWry42_zQ",
      "photo_credit": "Kamil Feczko"
    },
    {
      "text": "And every time, a soft pop answers from the far end of the room, like an echo.",
      "scene": "hallway",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1760387252429-fb4311fe0637?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "io8ALzlfrKk",
      "photo_credit": "MARIOLA GROBELSKA"
    },
    {
      "text": "Afterwards the hall always smells of a struck match. I blamed the candles.",
      "scene": "window",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1575060537120-ac5e96e1a16f?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "lrj7xeJlcb4",
      "photo_credit": "Anne Nygård"
    },
    {
      "text": "Then, editing the Hartley wedding, I saw a man sitting at a table near the front.",
      "scene": "table",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1783314867628-220ab03cac99?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "qePRtRzOUf0",
      "photo_credit": "Manya Sivanandam"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grey suit, hands folded over something black, staring straight into my lens.",
      "scene": "dark",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1505226755626-21044548b8aa?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "A545KXf87jE",
      "photo_credit": "Alexander Andrews"
    },
    {
      "text": "I'd walked that hall twice before the shot. Every seat was empty.",
      "scene": "hallway",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1762765684665-6b6855bb6fe6?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "jds_OTZ8c7w",
      "photo_credit": "Adrien Olichon"
    },
    {
      "text": "So I opened six years of empty rooms, every wedding I'd ever shot.",
      "scene": "note",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559057287-ce0f595679a8?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "toQNPpuDuwI",
      "photo_credit": "sue hughes"
    },
    {
      "text": "He was in all of them. Every venue. Every town.",
      "scene": "forest",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1534307965816-94396c7de0d2?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "ctJCaMBszqQ",
      "photo_credit": "Valery Sysoev"
    },
    {
      "text": "And in each one, he sat exactly one table closer to me.",
      "scene": "table",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792051533898-7b5c5d1d3f61?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "9TZq8xQ536E",
      "photo_credit": "Pix Tresa"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the very first, he was just a grey shape against the back wall.",
      "scene": "hallway",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1780385560539-c27d691a475e?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "INpIzz-Gz9c",
      "photo_credit": "Michael D Beckwith"
    },
    {
      "text": "Behind him, in every photo, sat the same small white flare, like a flash going off.",
      "scene": "dark",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608913916944-f957e585567e?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "ZDITQ5qsqlQ",
      "photo_credit": "El Swaggy"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hartleys' front table was the closest one. There were no tables left between us.",
      "scene": "table",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1790774889606-771f8d4552d1?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "YXruEoZ0CTU",
      "photo_credit": "Rakib Khan"
    },
    {
      "text": "And when I zoomed in, the black thing in his hands had a lens.",
      "scene": "dark",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516912926362-1da264f6c398?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "c1aghs7NngU",
      "photo_credit": "Nicolas Thomas"
    },
    {
      "text": "He was taking my photo at the exact moment I was taking his.",
      "scene": "window",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1570032678348-5a18c8a667ed?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "fUjbTb4liT0",
      "photo_credit": "Ed Vázquez"
    },
    {
      "text": "I stopped doing the empty room shot. I told couples I'd retired it.",
      "scene": "house",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551298328-a2f5d9f0b010?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "15RpelTxDls",
      "photo_credit": "Keith Polischuk"
    },
    {
      "text": "I sold that camera and bought a new one, still sealed in its box.",
      "scene": "dark",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516724562728-afc824a36e84?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "mS1nlYbq1kA",
      "photo_credit": "Robert Shunev"
    },
    {
      "text": "The man at the camera shop said ghost images are common on old sensors.",
      "scene": "door",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1664797523026-f6e277258f0c?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "mHuljON3bC8",
      "photo_credit": "Peter Herrmann"
    },
    {
      "text": "Three weddings went by, then four. No pop, no struck match, no man.",
      "scene": "forest",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1668166893230-bab2db9e4343?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "7fR24IUudk4",
      "photo_credit": "Rhamely"
    },
    {
      "text": "I started sleeping through the night again.",
      "scene": "house",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1624921938155-48a9a341d501?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "j-Vl5Ok5FCk",
      "photo_credit": "Brad Switzer"
    },
    {
      "text": "Then, at the Ashworth wedding, the last guests left, and the hall emptied around me.",
      "scene": "hallway",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1786062841848-18177898b3a7?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "zYDpQI4N_GU",
      "photo_credit": "Vishal Sinha"
    },
    {
      "text": "I was only checking a setting when I heard my own voice whisper, \"Last one.\"",
      "scene": "dark",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1697238724718-29cc8b1a2340?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "e_tSuzs7mqU",
      "photo_credit": "Taylor Burnfield"
    },
    {
      "text": "The shutter clicked. Pop. The room filled with the smell of a struck match.",
      "scene": "table",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1695641738244-25e5355e9a42?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "NWa1VZVPwjc",
      "photo_credit": "Benjamin Brunner"
    },
    {
      "text": "On the screen, he was out of his chair, standing in the aisle, an arm's length away.",
      "scene": "hallway",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1715534231620-670c16afc3a2?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "fxqc-gUnFek",
      "photo_credit": "Matt Richmond"
    },
    {
      "text": "As I left, the manager handed me an envelope. \"Your colleague left this for you.\"",
      "scene": "door",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1533719791354-582f7a7e136e?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "hQqIMb4uML8",
      "photo_credit": "CHRSNDRSN"
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside was an old black-and-white print of this same hall, decades ago.",
      "scene": "note",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1649019489428-70f505daacd6?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "Axli9F0n26A",
      "photo_credit": "Valeria Reverdo"
    },
    {
      "text": "I was in it, holding my camera, an arm's length from his lens.",
      "scene": "dark",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1522682178063-73ad4736e440?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "qw3TwCZ_jXg",
      "photo_credit": "Nik"
    },
    {
      "text": "On the back, in faded pencil: \"Last one.\"",
      "scene": "note",
      "photo": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1529066496421-d8fb2dca38a6?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb",
      "photo_id": "4Ujhq5_fJik",
      "photo_credit": "Annie Spratt"
    }
  ]
}